      {
        "title": "Ask HN: I have been unemployed for 2y. 15 years of experience, US. What to do?",
        "link": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50583761",
        "description": "<p>I'm Senior software engineer in the US (DMV area), with 15y of experience. Worked for Fortune 50+ company and bunch of mid-size companies. Been unemployed for 2y and can't find a job, within those 2 years, I pretty much spent my savings that I've saved through years, maybe have 4-5 months left to support my household. Currently, I tutor math and probably about to start working as manager in pizzaria.<p>In Jan 2025, I quit from a mid-size insurance tech company(1000+) after working there for almost 4y, because I was tipped off the they were about to start layoffs and they did. Well, since then I have zero luck finding any job in SWE.<p>At this point, I have massive gap in my resume that I can't explain to recruiters, I can still code (C#/.NET/AWS) and learned the AI, but who cares if date of my last employment is Jan2025. What should I do ?<p>If you have an alternative path (something completely different from SWE or SWE adjacent) that pays \"well\", I would like to hear.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50583761\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50583761</a></p>\n<p>Points: 78</p>\n<p># Comments: 81</p>",
        "pubDate": "Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:18:32 +0000",
        "guid": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50583761"
      },
